#!/bin/bash
# Track-level cleanup. Fires when the entire track ends (student
# completes or abandons it). Guarantees all DNS-AID records under
# this learner's per-sandbox subdomain are removed from Route 53,
# regardless of what they published.
#
# This is critical because:
#   - per-challenge cleanups only delete the records for that specific
#     agent name they know about
#   - students may publish extra capabilities (the optional second
#     dns-aid publish in C2 e.g. url-scanner)
#   - track timeout mid-challenge skips per-challenge cleanups
#
# Idempotent: missing records → no-op, missing zone → log and skip.
set -uo pipefail

source /opt/lab/lab.env 2>/dev/null || source /tmp/sandbox.env 2>/dev/null || {
    echo "[track-cleanup] no lab env present — nothing to clean"
    exit 0
}

: "${HOSTED_ZONE_ID:?missing}"
: "${SANDBOX_SLUG:?missing}"
: "${ZONE:?missing}"

SUBDOMAIN_SUFFIX=".${SANDBOX_SLUG}.${ZONE}."
echo "[track-cleanup] removing all records under *${SUBDOMAIN_SUFFIX}"

# 1. List every record under this sandbox's subdomain.
RECORDS=$(aws route53 list-resource-record-sets \
    --hosted-zone-id "${HOSTED_ZONE_ID}" \
    --query "ResourceRecordSets[?ends_with(Name, \`${SUBDOMAIN_SUFFIX}\`)]" \
    --output json 2>/dev/null || echo "[]")

COUNT=$(echo "${RECORDS}" | jq 'length')
if [ "${COUNT:-0}" = "0" ]; then
    echo "[track-cleanup] no records found — nothing to do"
    exit 0
fi
echo "[track-cleanup] found ${COUNT} record(s) to delete"

# 2. Build a single ChangeBatch with one DELETE per record. Submit
#    one call (Route53 max changes per call is 1000, plenty here).
CHANGES=$(echo "${RECORDS}" | jq '[.[] | {Action: "DELETE", ResourceRecordSet: .}]')
BATCH=$(jq -n --argjson changes "${CHANGES}" \
    '{Comment: "IETF lab track cleanup", Changes: $changes}')

aws route53 change-resource-record-sets \
    --hosted-zone-id "${HOSTED_ZONE_ID}" \
    --change-batch "${BATCH}" \
    --query 'ChangeInfo.{Status:Status,Id:Id}' --output table 2>&1 | sed 's/^/  /' || \
    echo "[track-cleanup] WARN: delete batch failed (probably already gone)"

echo "[track-cleanup] done"
exit 0
